  "apod": {
    "date": "2026-10-31",
    "title": "Night on a Spooky Planet",
    "explanation": " Explanation:   What spooky planet is this?  Planet Earth on a dark and stormy night, of course. The ghostly scene was  photographed at Hverir , a geothermally active area found along northeastern Iceland's  volcanic landscape . Triggered by  solar activity ,  geomagnetic storms  have unleashed energetic particles trapped in Earth's magnetic field. Penetrating the planet's upper atmosphere at high latitudes, the particles create  auroral displays  in the starry night sky. Ghostly towers of steam and gas are venting from  local fumaroles to dance  against the eerie, greenish northern lights. For now, auroral activity on planet Earth remains in a high state as the Sun is only in early phases of decline from the peak of its  solar activity cycle . And soon, other ghostly apparitions may dance in your neighborhood.  Happy Halloween !   Tomorrow's picture:   Sunday's Childe ",
    "image": "https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/Hverir_Vetter_1300.jpg?w=1300&h=867&fit=clip&crop=faces,focalpoint",
    "link": "https://science.nasa.gov/image-article/apod-2026-october-31-night-on-a-spooky-planet/",
    "credit": " Stéphane Vetter  ( Nuits sacrées )",
    "alt": "Steam is venting from volcanic fumaroles photographed against greenish aurorae.",
    "media_type": "image"
  },
  "updated": "2026-10-31T07:58:13.815170+00:00"
